.TH "VTTREGION.SCROLL" "3JS" "June 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VTTRegion.scroll \- VTTRegion: scroll property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]scroll\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R]
interface is an enumerated value indicating how existing cues in the
region move when a new cue is added.
.SH VALUE
A string.
Possible values are:
.TP
\f[B]\(dq\(dq\f[R] (the empty string)
Existing cues in the region don\(cqt scroll; instead, they are displayed
at the same time as new cues.
This is the default.
.TP
\f[B]\(dqup\(dq\f[R]
New cues are added at the bottom of the region, and existing cues scroll
upwards to make space for them.
.SH EXAMPLES
In the following example, a new \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] is created, then
the value of \f[CR]scroll\f[R] is set to \f[CR]\(dqup\(dq\f[R].
The value is then printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] region = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTRegion();
region.scroll = \(dqup\(dq;
console.log(region.scroll);
.EE
